# Recovery ueventd rules for the Qualcomm secure stack.
#
# ueventd's entry chain in this recovery: it parses /system/etc/ueventd.rc
# (provided by the build system, not this device tree) and imports
# /vendor/etc/ueventd.rc plus /odm/etc/ueventd.rc from there (observed in
# log/logcat.txt). This file is the ONLY ueventd config the device tree
# contributes; a ramdisk-root /ueventd.rc would never be parsed (ueventd has
# no such entry point) and was removed as dead config.
#
# QSEECom_start_app() loads the keymaster/gatekeeper TrustZone apps
# (keym2p.mdt, ...) with request_firmware(). The kernel firmware loader then
# asks ueventd, which searches the directories listed here in addition to the
# defaults (/etc/firmware, /odm/firmware, /vendor/firmware, /firmware/image).
# init.recovery.qcom.rc mounts the modem partition at /firmware in 'on fs', so
# the TA files are already reachable via the default /firmware/image path; the
# extra directory below is a belt-and-braces alias.
firmware_directories /firmware/image/
